From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000112 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:04:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] prompt cache: TF_DS_KEEP_PROTECT=1 supersedes a state only within its own
 conversation

Under fork fan-out victimBut freed a branch point first: ANY longer entry
extending its tokens counted as superseding it, so the parent
conversation re-prefilled its own prefix. And in dsv41's
lanes.placeKept the placement victim was the first kept state in keep
order, so the shared system-cut Snap (the oldest keep) was staled first
under pool pressure and every follower re-prefilled the shared prefix.
This patch covers both eviction layers of TF_DS_KEEP_PROTECT=1 (the
prompt-cache supersede rule and the placement victims).

With TF_DS_KEEP_PROTECT=1 (on only when exactly "1"; read where the store
is built, native/cuda.zig openWith and dsv41's lanes_main, and in
Lanes.init for placement) victimBut qualifies a superseder only when it
continues the state's own conversation: the same conversation group when
both carry one, else the lineage link (a descendant of its lineage
qualifies), and where neither link identifies the relation it counts as
before -- protection is never claimed on guesswork. Snap gains a shared
bit set through the prompt cache's new Snapshots.share vtable hook
(keepWith's shared paths: kept shared or promoted, and a restored shared
state at adopt, whose entry init marks the family copy too; GLM/flashnext
keep the null default), and placeKept takes a snap keptOver counts as
superseded first (any overlapping snap on a different base, or a longer
one on its own base), then the oldest non-shared snap, then the oldest
shared one. TF_DS_KEEP_PROTECT joins rank_identity's Features named
"keep_protect=1;" only when on (read in native.zig's rankExchange like
edit_mark), so an off pair's string is unchanged and a pair that
disagrees is refused at the hello.

Switch unset: victimBut's supersede formula and placeKept's
first-in-keep-order victim are behaviour-identical on the off path (one
inert Snap.shared write; read only under the switch); the shared and
skip exemptions and the placement candidate filters (non-stale,
non-loading, not source, non-clashing) are untouched, and no kernel
shapes change. Restore- and reserve-driven evictions (victimBut's call
sites without a conversation identity) pass no identity and keep base's
unprotected order.

Tests: zig build test and zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh pass; the patch's
own tests: prompt_cache_test.zig's same-group supersede first,
cross-group protection of the branch point, base order with the switch
unset and the lineage-link cases, lanes.zig's placeKept victims
(non-shared snaps before a shared one, the covered snap first, base order
unset), prompt_cache_tier_test.zig's restored shared state marking its
family copy at adopt, rank_identity.zig's keep_protect feature-string
shapes, and keepProtect's "1"-only parse. Not run on a pair.
---
